        "department": null,
        "description": "This course is aimed at students taking a first course in the subject of nonlinear dynamics and chaos. The course presentation stresses on analytical methods, concrete examples and geometric intuition. The theory is developed systematically, starting with first order differential equations and their bifurcations, followed by phase plane analysis, limit cycles and their bifurcations and leading to chaos, iterated maps, period doubling, fractals and strange attractors. Adequate emphasis is placed on physically motivated applications",
